data/languages/spc700core.sinc
data/languages/spc700ops.sinc

  SLEIGH decode table (registers, tokens, macros, and the 256 opcode
  constructors) for the Sony SPC700. The p-code semantics carried in these
  files are known-incorrect and are being rewritten by this project (bead
  grm-c9d.3); the decode table itself is what is vendored here.

  Copyright the SPCdra authors (https://github.com/qwertymodo/SPCdra)
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0

  Upstream: https://github.com/qwertymodo/SPCdra
  Commit:   295b552f768eb23abf601c46e27a6d5d3e10a03b
  Path:     data/languages/spc700.sinc (-> spc700core.sinc)
            data/languages/spc700-native.slaspec (-> spc700ops.sinc)

  This is a fork point, not a re-sync target: grm-c9d.3 rewrites the
  semantics on top of this decode table by design, so the files diverge
  permanently from upstream after that lands. Vendored verbatim at the
  commit above (spc700ops.sinc additionally drops upstream's leading
  "@include spc700.sinc" line, since our spc700.slaspec does the including);
  the only other modification is a prepended attribution header.
